{"id": "f29b9262-ed59-440a-a923-6a70b112377e", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This question really has two parts: figuring out why Bedrock latency got worse is an open-ended root-cause hunt, which calls for offering an investigation, while checking whether we have enough telemetry is a bounded question I can answer with a quick, lightweight survey.

I'll state the plan and spawn a subagent to do a telemetry inventory — checking Bedrock CloudWatch metrics like InvocationLatency and TimeToFirstToken, invocation logging config, CloudTrail, X-Ray/app logs, and model/account associations, starting with us-east-1 but checking other regions too. Once that inventory comes back, I can offer the deeper investigation as a follow-up.

"}]}

{"id": "617e2057-0612-482d-8997-0248769ba127", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Good question to settle before digging into the cause. I'll check what Bedrock telemetry you have: CloudWatch runtime metrics, invocation logging, tracing, and change history. Then I'll tell you whether it's enough to diagnose the slowdown.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_qx63Goc1mCZTI7C03NzBKo", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-telemetry-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "searching-logs", "exploring-traces", "discovering-topology"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Run a READ-ONLY inventory of what telemetry exists to diagnose Amazon Bedrock latency regressions, and assess whether it's sufficient. Do NOT try to find the root cause of the latency; only assess observability coverage and report what data is available.",
  "context": "User says Bedrock latency has gotten worse and they can't tell why. They ask: do we have enough telemetry to diagnose this? Agent space account is 012345678901_1, region us-east-1; also check any other associated AWS accounts (use list_associations) and any regions where Bedrock usage is evident. Current time is 2026-11-24T18:52Z.",
  "checks": [
    "CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock namespace: which metrics exist and for which ModelId dimensions (Invocations, InvocationLatency, TimeToFirstToken, InvocationClientErrors, InvocationServerErrors, InvocationThrottles, InputTokenCount, OutputTokenCount, EstimatedTPMQuotaUsage, etc.). Note data retention/recency and whether data points exist over the last 14 days. Give a quick sense of whether InvocationLatency trend shows a regression (just the headline numbers: e.g. p50/p90/avg last 24h vs prior 7d per model), without root-causing.",
    "Bedrock model invocation logging: is it enabled (GetModelInvocationLoggingConfiguration)? Destinations (CloudWatch Logs group / S3), whether text/image/embedding delivery is on, and whether the log group/bucket has recent data.",
    "Application-side telemetry: Lambda/ECS/EKS/EC2 callers of Bedrock (topology or log groups mentioning bedrock), whether they emit logs/custom metrics with latency, and whether X-Ray / OTel tracing covers Bedrock calls.",
    "Change history: whether CloudTrail records (Bedrock InvokeModel/Converse management/data events, config changes like provisioned throughput, guardrails, inference profiles, cross-region inference) are available and queryable for the last 14 days.",
    "Other signals: Service Quotas for Bedrock (throttling/TPM/RPM), guardrails configured, provisioned throughput, cross-region inference profiles, any CloudWatch alarms/dashboards on Bedrock, and any third-party observability associations (Datadog, Grafana, etc.) that could hold Bedrock data."
  ],
  "output": "Concise report: per signal -> available / partial / missing, with specific resource names (log groups, buckets, model IDs, regions). Then a verdict on sufficiency, a list of gaps, and what could be diagnosed vs. not. Keep it brief."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit Bedrock telemetry coverage: metrics, logs, traces, change history"}], "created_at": null}

